      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Greenhorn,_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Greenhorn began as a gold mining boomtown in the 1860s and was originally known as Robinsonville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Greenhorn,_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Oregon Legislature officially designated Greenhorn as a historic ghost town in 1983.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
